Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• actor.actor_id, actor.first_name, actor.last_name: identify each actor and display their names.  
• film_actor.actor_id, film_actor.film_id: links an actor to every film she/he appears in.  
• film.film_id, film.title: film catalogue, needed only for readability.  
• inventory.film_id, inventory.inventory_id: transforms a film into the physical items that are rented.  
• rental.inventory_id, rental.customer_id: turns every inventory item into actual rentals and the customer who rented it.  
• customer.customer_id: used to count either (1) all customers or (2) the customers that appear in rentals of the selected actors’ films.  

Typical conditions / filters that will be applied  

• GROUP BY film_actor.actor_id ORDER BY COUNT(*) DESC LIMIT 5       – to isolate the five “top” actors (by number of rentals).  
• WHERE film_actor.actor_id IN ( … top‑5 list … )                  – to keep only those actors in further joins.  
• DISTINCT customer.customer_id                                      – each customer should be counted once.  

Below are ten exploratory → final SQL queries (SQLite), each one different and limited to 20 rows where result sets can grow:

```sql
-- 1. Description: inspect all actors (id, name) so we know the dimension of the table.
SELECT DISTINCT
       a.actor_id,
       a.first_name,
       a.last_name
FROM   actor AS a
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: look at the raw link between actors and films.
SELECT DISTINCT
       fa.actor_id,
       fa.film_id
FROM   film_actor AS fa
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: count the number of films each actor appears in (top‑20 shown).
SELECT fa.actor_id,
       COUNT(*) AS film_count
FROM   film_actor AS fa
GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
ORDER  BY film_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: rank actors by the number of rentals generated by their films (top‑20).
SELECT
       fa.actor_id,
       COUNT(*) AS rental_count
FROM   film_actor  AS fa
JOIN   inventory   AS i  ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
JOIN   rental      AS r  ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
ORDER  BY rental_count DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: store the TOP‑5 actors (by rental count) in a CTE and list them with names.
WITH top5 AS (
     SELECT fa.actor_id
     FROM   film_actor AS fa
     JOIN   inventory  AS i ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental     AS r ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
     ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
     LIMIT 5
)
SELECT t.actor_id,
       a.first_name,
       a.last_name
FROM   top5 AS t
JOIN   actor AS a USING (actor_id)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: how many distinct customers are in the whole database?
SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id) AS total_customers
FROM   customer
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: fetch every customer that has rented ANY film featuring one of the top‑5 actors.
WITH top5 AS (
     SELECT fa.actor_id
     FROM   film_actor AS fa
     JOIN   inventory  AS i ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental     AS r ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
     ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
     LIMIT 5
)
SELECT DISTINCT
       c.customer_id
FROM   top5        AS t
JOIN   film_actor  AS fa ON fa.actor_id = t.actor_id
JOIN   inventory   AS i  ON i.film_id   = fa.film_id
JOIN   rental      AS r  ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
JOIN   customer    AS c  ON c.customer_id  = r.customer_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: compute the single number of customers that rented those films.
WITH top5 AS (
     SELECT fa.actor_id
     FROM   film_actor AS fa
     JOIN   inventory  AS i ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental     AS r ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
     ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
     LIMIT 5
),
cust AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT
            c.customer_id
     FROM   top5        AS t
     JOIN   film_actor  AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = t.actor_id
     JOIN   inventory   AS i  ON i.film_id    = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental      AS r  ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     JOIN   customer    AS c  ON c.customer_id  = r.customer_id
)
SELECT COUNT(*) AS customers_who_rented_top5
FROM   cust
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: percentage of customer base that rented films with the top‑5 actors.
WITH
top5 AS (
     SELECT fa.actor_id
     FROM   film_actor AS fa
     JOIN   inventory  AS i ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental     AS r ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
     ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
     LIMIT 5
),
cust_top5 AS (
     SELECT DISTINCT
            c.customer_id
     FROM   top5        AS t
     JOIN   film_actor  AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = t.actor_id
     JOIN   inventory   AS i  ON i.film_id    = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental      AS r  ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     JOIN   customer    AS c  ON c.customer_id  = r.customer_id
),
tot AS (
     SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT customer_id) AS n_all
     FROM   customer
),
hit AS (
     SELECT COUNT(*) AS n_hit
     FROM   cust_top5
)
SELECT
       hit.n_hit  * 100.0 / tot.n_all  AS pct_customers_renting_top5_actors
FROM   hit, tot
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--10. Description: list the names of customers (sample 20) who rented at least one film with any of the top‑5 actors.
WITH top5 AS (
     SELECT fa.actor_id
     FROM   film_actor AS fa
     JOIN   inventory  AS i ON i.film_id      = fa.film_id
     JOIN   rental     AS r ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
     GROUP  BY fa.actor_id
     ORDER  BY COUNT(*) DESC
     LIMIT 5
)
SELECT DISTINCT
       c.customer_id,
       c.first_name,
       c.last_name
FROM   top5        AS t
JOIN   film_actor  AS fa ON fa.actor_id  = t.actor_id
JOIN   inventory   AS i  ON i.film_id    = fa.film_id
JOIN   rental      AS r  ON r.inventory_id = i.inventory_id
JOIN   customer    AS c  ON c.customer_id  = r.customer_id
LIMIT 20;
```

Run the queries in sequence; the last two will give you:

• customers_who_rented_top5 and total_customers → you can calculate the percentage, or  
• pct_customers_renting_top5_actors directly, showing the widespread appeal of the top five actors.
